00:25:36,150 --> 00:25:36,930
Always a tricky one.

463
00:25:37,330 --> 00:25:41,120
Our sources highlight a situation where supplier problems are threatening a deadline.

464
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:42,680
How do you handle that?

465
00:25:42,700 --> 00:25:47,050
You know, that delicate balance between the client wanting it now and these unexpected issues.

466
00:25:47,210 --> 00:25:52,190
Right, and this really brings up the question, what do you do when a supplier just can't get you the materials on time?

467
00:25:52,430 --> 00:25:55,820
The key thing here, the sources suggest, is to look at the critical path again.

468
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,000
Really dig into it.

469
00:25:57,020 --> 00:25:58,180
The critical path, right?

470
00:25:58,200 --> 00:26:01,220
The sequence of tasks that dictates the whole timeline.

471
00:26:01,310 --> 00:26:01,810
Exactly.

472
00:26:01,970 --> 00:26:04,430
And you try to find places where you can genuinely save time.

473
00:26:04,810 --> 00:26:07,110
It's not just about pushing the deadline back.

474
00:26:07,450 --> 00:26:09,240
It's a strategic rethink.

475
00:26:09,260 --> 00:26:10,160
Can we shuffle things?

476
00:26:10,260 --> 00:26:11,580
Can we do things in parallel?

477
00:26:12,180 --> 00:26:14,700
